.TH CHESSCAN-GUI 1 "November 2026" "chesscan 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chesscan-gui \- desktop chess board scanner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chesscan-gui
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Desktop front end for
.BR chesscan (1).
It captures the screen, finds the chess board, reads the position into FEN,
queries a UCI engine and shows the best lines, the evaluation and the winning
probability. The best move is drawn as an arrow on a live preview of the board.
.PP
The window is a normal desktop window, so it can be moved, resized, minimised
and switched between like any other application. With
.B \-\-overlay
it becomes a small always-on-top panel instead, for use while playing.
.PP
Detecting and calibrating hide the window for a moment before capturing the
screen, so the scanner never mistakes its own window for the board.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-overlay
Small borderless always-on-top panel instead of the full window: win
percentage, evaluation bar, the top engine lines, a side-to-move flip,
a re-detect button and start/stop. Drag it by its handle; the position is
remembered.
.TP
.B \-\-auto
Detect the board and start scanning as soon as the window opens.
.TP
.B \-\-calibrate
Detect the board and open the calibration dialog.
.TP
.BI \-\-pos " X,Y"
Place the window at those screen coordinates. Overrides the remembered
overlay position.
.SH GETTING STARTED
.PP
.nf
  1. Launch chesscan-gui
  2. Press "Detect board"
  3. Press "Calibrate" once per board theme, label the clusters, Apply
  4. Press "Start scanning"
.fi
.PP
Calibration is needed once per theme, resolution and board size. It clusters
the 64 squares and shows what each cluster actually looks like, so labelling is
a look rather than a guess.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/chesscan/config.json
Board rectangle, engine settings and learned piece prototypes. Set
.B CHESSCAN_CONFIG
to use another file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chesscan (1),
.BR stockfish (6)